  "acceptance": "Discharge one more of the D3/D7 '...Statement' Props of blocker I4 on an honest, constructed domain, and produce the first machine-checked inventory of which Props are now proved/model/statement-only. Context: release/Poincare/Longrun/Entropy/Bridge.lean defines six Props (WeightedIBPStatement, WeightedLaplacianStatement, BochnerStatement, ConjugateMeasureEvolutionStatement, FDerivativeStatement, EntropyFunctionalRegularityStatement) over WeightedCalculus/EntropyData. D13 already: proves WeightedLaplacianStatement unrestricted on the Euclidean chart, proves the flat Bochner identity, proves the Gaussian pointwise conjugate-heat equation and a clamped-lifetime F-monotonicity, and kernel-checks that the unrestricted WeightedIBPStatement is FALSE. Required content: (1) build an explicit family E : R -> EntropyData X mu (X finite type with counting measure, or the D13 backward-Gaussian model) with an explicit closed-form F and prove EntropyFunctionalRegularityStatement for it (ContDiffOn R 1 (fun s => (E s).F) (Ici 0)); (2) show a downstream consumer: feed the discharged statement into the existing entropy bridge structure (Poincare/Longrun/Entropy/Bridge.lean entropyRegularityBridge or the D13 certificate layer) and derive a corollary that was not available before (e.g. an explicit derivative/lifetime statement), so the discharge is genuinely used; (3) emit a machine-checked inventory module with one theorem per each of the six Props classifying it as proved-unrestricted / proved-on-domain / false-unrestricted / statement-only, each with its exact domain hypotheses, and state explicitly that no manifold-level statement is claimed. Acceptance evidence: compiling modules, source hashes, compile exits, fail-closed axiom audit cones subset {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, non-vacuous witness for the discharged statement, a kernel-checked counterexample or domain restriction note for any statement left open, and an adversarial semantic review confirming the inventory is accurate. Do NOT weaken or restate any Prop; proving a restricted form is allowed only when the restriction is explicit in the theorem name and docstring.",
  "expected_evidence": "compiled discharge of EntropyFunctionalRegularityStatement + downstream corollary + six-Prop inventory with classifications + witnesses + hashes/exits/axiom audit + semantic review; semantic class model (finite/Gaussian) versus statement-only, explicitly not a manifold entropy theorem",
